# WHAT VERCEL IS ALLOWED TO SEE, AND WHY THIS FILE IS NOT OPTIONAL.
#
# THE VERCEL CLI DOES NOT READ `.gitignore`. That is the whole reason this file exists, and the
# first deploy of this project is what proved it: `Dump20260622.sql` is 194 MB, is listed in
# `.gitignore`, is untracked by git — and was uploaded anyway, in a 229 MB payload that failed on
# Vercel's 100 MB per-file limit.
#
# THE SIZE WAS THE SYMPTOM AND NOT THE PROBLEM. That file is the raw source database extract. It is
# an INPUT to `tools/etl/build.py`, which compiles it down into the small binaries under
# `public/data` that the app actually fetches. Uploading it to a static host would have published
# the entire source database at a public URL. The 100 MB limit refused the deploy for the wrong
# reason and did the right thing.
#
# ANYTHING ADDED HERE MUST NOT BE A BUILD INPUT. Vercel runs `npm run build` on what it receives,
# so `src/`, `public/`, `index.html`, the tsconfigs, `vite.config.ts` and the manifests all have to
# survive. Checked before excluding: nothing under `src/` imports from `tools/`, `_planning/` or
# `docs/`, so none of the three is reachable from the build graph.

# ── the source extract, and any other dump dropped beside it ──────────────────
*.sql

# ── build artefacts Vercel regenerates itself ─────────────────────────────────
# `dist` is the OUTPUT of the build command, so shipping it is 20 MB of round trip for a directory
# that gets overwritten. `node_modules` is 177 MB and is reinstalled from the lockfile.
node_modules
dist

# ── working material that is not the product ──────────────────────────────────
# Design studies, session notes, the ETL, and the local agent config. `_planning` alone is 2.1 MB
# of standalone HTML explorations that no route serves.
_planning
tools
docs
.claude

# ── local machine noise ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
*.local
